  2141	# PLAN-161 U3 (codex r4 F2): find(1) resolves its COMMAND-LINE path through
  2142	# symlinked ANCESTORS even without -L — only descent below the start point is
  2143	# no-follow. So a nominated excluded tree whose ancestor (e.g. .claude/hooks
  2144	# preserved via --skip as an adopter symlink) is a symlink would be walked —
  2145	# and, once any purge elsewhere makes _PM_PURGED_COUNT positive, rmdir'd —
  2146	# INSIDE the symlink's external target. Guard: before any find/rmdir over a
  2147	# nominated path, walk every component from $TARGET down to the leaf with a
  2148	# per-component lstat (same idiom as _baseline_relpath_unsafe) and refuse the
  2149	# whole tree when ANY component is a symlink. On hit, prints the first
  2150	# symlinked component's target-relative path to stdout and returns 0; returns
  2151	# 1 when the component chain is symlink-free. bash-3.2-safe (IFS walk).
