   652	
   653	## Post-install: configure env vars (optional but recommended)
   654	
   655	The framework ships with safe defaults — most adopters can run as-is.
   656	But for production-like installs you should configure 2 categories:
   657	
   658	**1. Budget controls** (prevents runaway autonomous-session cost):
   659	
   660	```bash
   661	export CEO_BUDGET_ENFORCE=1
   662	export CEO_BUDGET_PER_SPAWN=0.25            # USD per single sub-agent spawn
   663	export CEO_BUDGET_BYPASS_MAX_PER_DAY=1      # tighten to 1 in production
   664	```
   665	
   666	**2. State path** (only if you want state outside `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/`):
   667	
   668	```bash
   669	export CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR=/srv/ceo-state/$USER
   670	```
   671	
   672	For the **complete catalog (~55+ env-vars)** organized in 6 categories
   673	(Hook kill-switches, Behavioral kill-switches, Diagnostic, Activation
   674	opt-ins, Budget/Cost, Path/Storage):
   675	
   676	- [`docs/GOVERNANCE.md`](docs/GOVERNANCE.md) §"What CAN be turned off"
   677	  is the canonical reference.
   678	- [`docs/DAY-1-CHECKLIST.md`](docs/DAY-1-CHECKLIST.md) §Step 11
   679	  has the day-1 emergency-only top-7 picks.
   680	- [`docs/CHEAT-SHEET.md`](docs/CHEAT-SHEET.md) is the single-page
   681	  cheat-sheet for daily use.
   682	
   683	**Frozen invariants** that env-vars CANNOT bypass: VETO floor model
   684	assignment (ADR-052), canonical-edit sentinel discipline (ADR-031),
   685	kernel-override audit emit (ADR-031 §kernel-override), and Claude-only
   686	positioning (ADR-085). These are auditable security floors —
   687	no env-var overrides them.
